nk it's safe to say  that the event is more about high  performance than the whole peak aspect  of it now before i get into what we  could possibly see in terms of a new  chip let me first refresh you guys on  what we should be expecting to see  tomorrow  first off we're going to be getting a  new iphone sc3 and according to sources  like ross young and michiko it's going  to have the same 4.7 inch display the  same home button and the same overall  design except with the new a15 chip and  5g support and we should also be  expecting a new ipad air 5 with the a15  chip 5g and potentially some features  like quad stereo speakers a new dual  camera design and a new purple color  according to luke miyani and on top of  that the iphone 13 is supposed to get a  new green color as well as a bunch of  new cases but all of that right there  isn't what this event is truly going to  be about because we're about to see a  bunch of new mac related products so  let's jump right into these leaks  first up we've been expecting apple's  new high-end mac mini ever since late  last year when it was delayed because  apple wanted to give more attention to  the new macbook pros so i fully believe  that we'll be seeing this new mac mini  at tomorrow's event packing the same m1  pro and m1 max chips that we already  have in the new macbook pros but other  than that apple did actually register  two more mac devices with the eec which  means that we could see these new macs  revealed at this event and thankfully we  got some huge leaks over the weekend  first up dan rue posted a tweet  mentioning that he heard from a source  that we could be getting a higher end  imac at this event but the weird thing  is that ming chakrow just tweeted his  expectations for mac releases this year  including a more powerful mac mini which  we were expecting and a new 27-inch  non-mini led display this year and then  both the imac pro and mac pro next year  and the key point is that ross young was  actually expecting the imac pro here in  the next couple of months as well as dan  rui who says an imac could be coming  tomorrow so in my opinion what we could  actually be seeing is a new 27-inch  high-end imac that is not an imac pro  but a new imac to fit the same m1 pro  and m1 max chips as the new high-end mac  mini will be getting and the craziest  thing of all is that over the weekend  mark german's power on newsletter  finally for the first time acknowledged  the possibility of having two different  27-inch imacs which is something that  i've been considering for months now and  he says we could be seeing a new imac  perhaps as soon as the first half of the  year while at the same time he doesn't  believe a new mac pro or imac pro is  ready to go on sale imminently matching  up to what mingxiquo said so with all of  that said a new imac is definitely a  possibility for tomorrow but on top of  that we got some major leaks this  morning in terms of apple releasing a  new studio 27 inch display tomorrow and  almost every source agrees with this  first of all nine to five max shared  some exclusive leaks late last week  concerning this new display coming  alongside a new mac studio which i'm  about to get into after this display and  then of course ming chakra already  mentioned it and then mark german  actually mentioned the same display  saying that apple has completed work on  it months ago and it could be ready to  launch at any moment even tomorrow but  then luke miani came out with some  exclusive leaks this morning saying that  he fully believes that this display is  coming at tomorrow's event and i think  with everything that we've been seeing  this display is coming for sure no doubt  about it and now before i get into the  absolute most surprising reveal at  tomorrow's event including my theory on  what it would actually be let me first  talk about the new expected m2 chip for  weeks now we've been getting a lot of  leaks concerning a new entry-level  macbook pro coming at this event  starting with a digit times report  earlier this year which at first didn't  really make any sense until more and  more leaks started to confirm this idea  especially the fact that one of the max  apple registered with the eec was  actually a laptop and then this weekend  mark german took things to a whole new  level by mentioning that apple has been  testing out multiple macs with a new  chip in recent weeks that includes an 8  core cpu and 10 core gpu which are  exactly the specs for the m2 chip  according to mark german and apparently  apple has been testing this new chip on  machines running mac os 12.3 12.4 and  the future mac os 13. so the idea is  that if apple was not planning on  releasing these new m2 max until wwdc  then why would they be testing it with a  version of mac os that's supposed to be  getting released as soon as next week  and then going further mark believes  that we'll be getting both m2 and m1 pro  m1 max model max all coming in the first  half of this year including mac minis  with both of those chips imax with up to  the m1 max and a new macbook pro with an  m2 chip all being spread out over the  next couple of months up until june so  before i give you my take on which ones  are coming when let's jump right into  the new mac studio this new mac showed  up last week with an exclusive leak from  9 to 5 mac claiming that it would sit  somewhere between the mac mini and the  mac pro and then luke miani came out  this morning and claimed that the new  max studio would be revealed at  tomorrow's event no doubt about it and i  actually believe him so let me explain  why first up 9 to 5 max says that apple  is working on two different versions of  this new mac studio with one of them  getting up to an m1 max chip while the  other will be getting an even more  powerful chip potentially the m1 max duo  and at first this was really weird to me  because i thought that the new high-end  mac mini was supposed to get the m1 pro  and m1 max chips so it wouldn't really  make sense for the max studio to also  start with the m1 max until i realized  something that should have been obvious  to me the entire time  what if this new mac studio is actually  the replacement for the high-end mac  mini because if you think about it the  redesigned mac mini renders that we were  seeing from sources like john prosser  and leeks apple pro came with a much  slimmer design language and the weirdest  part of all is that the cooling system  on those renders seemed to be inferior  for being able to cool the m1 max so  what if that new slim design is actually  only meant for the new lower end m2 chip  which uses a lot less power and that  would mean that apple would need a new  much larger mac mini design with  sufficient cooling capabilities exactly  like luke miyani's render show us with  tons of vents on the bottom being  perfect for the m1 max or maybe even an  m1 max duo and the idea i have is that  because this new design is much larger  than the mac mini apple cannot call it a  mini anymore and they also can't call it  a mac mini pro since it still has the  name mini in it and therefore they need  a brand new title the mac studio and in  my point of view this would make it a  lot easier for apple to market this new  mac because in the past there used to be  both a low end and a high-end mac mini  so it could get confusing if you're  trying to figure out if it's the weak  version or the powerful version but now  a mac studio will always be known as the  high-end pro version and the mac mini  will always be known as the lower end  consumer friendly version and since i  believe the mac studio is quite  literally the new high-end mac mini i  can basically guarantee that it is  coming tomorrow and with that said if  the new 27-inch apple display is in fact  called the studio display then it will  also 100 get released alongside the mac  studio because it just makes sense for  marketing but now we've got to 